Z||000000||KRMFiero||10-30-2001||10:21 PM||||Im looking to build up a Performance Caddy 4.5 Engine, It will be completly rebuilt, I want to get a turbo for it, i have been looking at turbos and eather they will wind up to fast or will produce to much boast,<BR>anyways It is a V-8, I dont want more then 7PSI boast, I want say 5PSI... <BR>Would 4cyl turbos work or whould they rev up to fast? turbo off like a 6cyl Reagle?  I dont want to put to much boost... Whats the differance between a Gas and Deisel turbo besides were the intake goes to<P>Kyle||||reg||5
Z||000001||Turbo88||10-31-2001||03:15 PM||||Let me see if I can help answer your question. For that engine you would need to use either a really large T3 or a small T04. A Grand National turbo would work but be slightly undersized (spin to fast). The flipside is if you buy a turbo with a wastegate or get an external wastegate, you won't have an over-boosting problem. The wastegate will allow the exhaust exhaust pressure to skip the turbo all together. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Neal||10-31-2001||06:21 PM||||Ideally you want the turbo to spool up as fast as possible and still make max boost at max RPM.<P>Even with 5psi i think ANY T3 youll find will be too small.  Id look for a used supra turbo, should be about the right size for a low boosted caddy V8.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pureSKID||11-07-2001||07:38 PM||||The supra single turbo uses the CT26 turbo... same one as the MR2.<BR>This is a large T3 size turbo.||||reg||1
